  "findings": [
    "Single-scene workload adopts 61 actions (65 facts); action62 invokes injected generation once then cannot assemble independent review. A legitimate scene change makes this particular coordinator context fit again.",
    "Explicit scene changes every20 actions retain all facts but only84 actions (88 facts) fit; action85 cannot assemble actor input, with zero producer/reviewer calls. Storage fact cap200 is not the first failure.",
    "Sixteen promises are individually declared and fulfilled through the durable path. Promise17 invokes injected generation but is rejected by history capacity before review; all prior promises are resolved and retained.",
    "The three failed candidates change no runtime state; world content is unchanged. Each original plus branch is verified through export/import/reopen."
  ],
  "nextImplementation": [
    "Define versioned current-state/history separation and protected dependency closure before changing storage/reader behavior. Preserve original fact and event identities.",
    "Govern historical selection by role visibility, unresolved obligations, discovery prerequisites, actual candidate references and recorded manifests. Missing mandatory evidence must stop; omitted history must not be treated as absent.",
    "Address fact/goal/thread growth and resolved promise history together. Do not merely raise constants, silently prune settled records or count filler dialogue as sustained narrative.",
    "Verify100/300/1000 consequence-bearing engineering actions, more than16 resolved promises and more than32 goals, then separately evaluate real-model and human long conversations."
  ],
